// =====================================================================================================================================
// File          : TestDataVault.java
// Package       : utilities
// Description   : The "jar" of test data, filled BEFORE the first browser opens and emptied row by row during the run.
//
//                 Why: every ENTS / BISS test case used to run its Oracle queries in the middle of the scenario (5-6 s
//                 each, one after the other) and only found out that a herd was unusable after login and navigation.
//                 The vault holds the rows of every query up front, with a status per row, so a test case takes a row
//                 from memory in a millisecond and a bad row is skipped instead of failing the run.
//
//                 Files (runtime-data/vault/, never committed - they hold farmer names and herds):
//                   herds.csv   one row per herd: pool,key,herd,name,address,login,status,test_case,purpose,reason,fetched_at,updated_at
//                   people.csv  one row per login: login,type,status,last_checked,note
//                   vault.meta  when the jar was filled + the database fingerprints at that moment
//                   TestDataVault_view.xlsx  a copy of both tables for people to open in Excel (never read back)
//                   archive/<date>/           the previous jar, moved aside when the jar is refilled
//
//                 Pools (pool / key):
//                   ENTS_AGENT        / agent login   herds of one agent with entitlements   (ENTS Agent Login herds)
//                   ENTS_ETF          / partner login herds linked to one ETF partner          (ENTS ETF partner herds)
//                                                     - ETF partners are not in herd_agt, so an agent pool that comes
//                                                       back empty is fetched again as an ETF pool (01-10-2026)
//                   ENTS_NO_ENTS      / agent login   herds of one agent WITHOUT entitlements (TC_02_ENTS negative case)
//                   ENTS_INDIVIDUAL   / -             herds whose holder has an online login  (ENTS Individual Login herds)
//                   BISS_NOT_STARTED  / scheme year   Not Started agent herds + INET agent login
//                   BISS_IND_CISYF    / scheme year   Not Started individual CISYF herds + the holder's own login
//
//                 Statuses: AVAILABLE -> RESERVED (a test has taken it) -> USED (the test finished with it)
//                                                                       -> BAD  (it failed a check; the reason is kept)
//                 A RESERVED row is never handed out again, so a run that stops halfway cannot pass a half-used herd
//                 to the next run. release() puts a RESERVED row back only when nothing was done with it.
//
//                 Freshness (isStale): the jar is refilled when
//                   - data.force.refresh=true
//                   - it was filled before the most recent data.refresh.day (default MONDAY - the weekly DB refresh)
//                   - a database fingerprint stored in vault.meta no longer matches (DataHarvester checks this)
//
//                 Settings (application.properties, all optional):
//                   data.vault.enabled=true            false = the test cases query Oracle as before
//                   data.vault.dir=runtime-data/vault
//                   data.refresh.day=MONDAY
//                   data.force.refresh=false
//                   data.low.stock=5                   stock report warns below this many AVAILABLE rows
//
//                 Thread safety: every public method is synchronized, and herds.csv is written under a file lock
//                 (vault.lock) so two framework processes on one machine cannot both take the same herd.
//
// Author        : Aniket Pathare | aniket.pathare@government.ie
// Date Created  : 01-10-2026
// =====================================================================================================================================

